parts.text:
The user wants: when selecting photos from Google Photos, allow categorizing photos based on the menu pages. And only show photos that belong to the menu pages.

Interpretation: After picking photos via Google Photos Picker, the user should be able to assign/categorize each picked photo to a menu page (Home, Canada, Colombia, Trips, Simon Family, General Family, Gallery, Her Story). Then each page only shows the photos categorized for that page. "Solamente muestra las fotos que son para las paginas del menu" = only show the photos that are for the menu pages (i.e., don't show uncategorized ones; each page shows only its assigned photos).

So we need a UI for categorizing selected photos. Implementation options:

1. After picking, show a categorization modal/section where each picked photo has a dropdown to choose the page. Store assignments in sessionStorage (and maybe localStorage). Then each page's gallery/placeholders show only photos assigned to that page.

2. Since selected photos are stored in sessionStorage and base URLs expire, keep that behavior.

We need:
- A modal with the picked photos (thumbnails), each with a `<select>` of pages, defaulting maybe to "Galería" or unassigned. Buttons "Guardar" / "Cancelar". On save, store `page` field per item.
- Only show photos with a page assignment on the corresponding page. "Solamente muestra las fotos que son para las páginas del menú" could also mean: only show photos that are assigned to menu pages (exclude unassigned). So pages show only their category.
- If the user picks photos and doesn't categorize, maybe assign to Gallery by default? Better to require selection or default "Photo Gallery". Hmm.

Let's design:
- `PAGE_ORDER` already maps files. Add labels:
  ```js
  const PAGE_INFO = [
    { file: "index.html", label: "Home" },
    { file: "canada.html", label: "Memories of Canada" },
    { file: "colombia.html", label: "Memories of Colombia" },
    { file: "trips.html", label: "Trips & Adventures" },
    { file: "simon-family.html", label: "Family of Simon" },
    { file: "family.html", label: "Our General Family" },
    { file: "gallery.html", label: "Photo Gallery" },
    { file: "story.html", label: "Her Story" },
  ];
  ```
- `photosForPage` becomes filtering by `item.page === currentFile` instead of rotation. But then pages with no assigned photos would be empty. That's expected: "solamente muestra las fotos que son para las páginas del menú". We could fall back to rotation if no photos assigned to that page? The requirement says only show photos for the pages. So filter strictly. But then if the user categorizes only some, other pages show nothing. Maybe show a message "No hay fotos asignadas a esta página."

- Categorization UI: after `pickPhotos` returns items, show a modal with each photo and a `<select>` (options: the 8 pages, plus maybe "No mostrar"). Default: infer from filename? No. Default to "gallery.html" maybe. Better default "index.html"? Hmm. Let's default to "gallery.html" (Photo Gallery) as a catch-all, but user can change. Or default to the current page. Since they clicked sync on index, default to index? Not great. I'll default to "gallery.html" and provide a "No mostrar" option (empty). The user explicitly categorizes.

